# Backend API Conventions

## Structure
- Controllers in `com.efiscal.backend.controller`
- Business logic in `com.efiscal.backend.service`
- JPA Entities in `com.efiscal.backend.model`
- Repositories in `com.efiscal.backend.repository`
- Config & Security in `com.efiscal.backend.config` and `com.efiscal.backend.security`

## Authentication
- Most endpoints require JWT Bearer token via `BearerTokenFilter`
- Use Spring Security annotations or filter logic for protected routes
- Granular Role-Based Access Control (RBAC): Enforce action-based permissions (e.g. `FISCAL_CREATE_BILL`) and client/organization scope bounds.

## Error Responses
- Adhere to the API Error Model defined in `API_CONTRACT.md`
- Use consistent HTTP status codes:
  - 400: Validation/Bad Request
  - 401: Unauthorized (Invalid/missing token)
  - 403: Forbidden (Missing role/scope or expired subscription)
  - 404: Resource not found
  - 500: Internal server error

## Patterns
- DTO pattern for request/response bodies (do not expose internal entities directly to controllers)
- Password hashing: BCryptPasswordEncoder
- Idempotency-Key support required for mutating fiscal endpoints to avoid duplicate submissions
